entries.english:
Georg Karl [von Fechenbach], Bishop zu Würzburg, grants Johann Friedrich Karl Philipp von Rosenbach the following properties as male fiefs, following the death of his predecessor Franz Ludwig [von Erthal]:
- Thundorf Castle, with all rights, appurtenances, and revenues, except only the farmyard;
- the deserted settlement of Ransbach, with its mill and farm, and all rights and revenues;
- the villages of Theinfeld and Rothhausen, with all rights, possessions, and revenues there;
- an estate in Maßbach behind the churchyard;
- the estates in Poppenlauer;
- the estates in Ebertshausen;
- half the tithe at Altenmünster;
- one third of the tithe at Oberlauringen;
- one eighth of the tithe at Alsleben;
- one quarter of the tithe at Ober- and Untereßfeld;
- a vineyard and two wooded plots at Thundorf.

In addition, the bishop grants them the following properties, which had belonged outright to Veit Ulrich von Schaumberg, who then enfeoffed them to the Prince-Bishopric of Würzburg:
- the farmyard and vineyards at Thundorf;
- the lake at Weißensee;
- a fishing right in the Lauer below Maßbach;
- a fishing right in the Lauer within the Rothhausen district;
- three quarters of the mill at Rothhausen;
- two estates at Theinfeld;
- two freehold estates at Weichtungen;
- four rent fiefs at Stadtlauringen;
- nine estates and eleven fiefs in Maßbach;
- the Brandmühle below Maßbach;
- five estates and four fiefs in Poppenlauer;
- three estates and one fief in Nüdlingen;
- one fief in Rannungen;
- a field estate in Hesselbach;
- the Herlingsberg wood;
- the male fief at Prappach.
These properties were purchased from the brothers Georg Dietrich, Wilhelm Ludwig, Wilhelm Ulrich, Georg Wilhelm, Johann Sigmund, Johann Philipp, and Johann Wilhelm von Schaumburg.

Finally, the bishop also grants them the following properties, which had originally been fiefs of the County of Henneberg and subsequently of the Duchy of Saxe-Weimar, and which passed to Würzburg under an agreement between the Prince-Bishopric of Würzburg and the Duchy of Saxe-Weimar:
- the Zent court at Maßbach, subsequently transferred to Poppenlauer, with all appurtenances and rights, excluding the villages of Maßbach and Volkershausen;
- half of the bailiwick at Poppenlauer;
- two estates in Maßbach and a meadow between Maßbach and Rothhausen;
- one quarter of the tithe at Zeil am Main;
- one third of a small quarter of the wine tithe at Zeil am Main;
- one third and one quarter of a full quarter of the wine tithe at Zeil am Main;
- four wooded plots near Maßbach;
- the wine rents and rent revenues at Schonungen. If the von Rosenbach family should ever have no male heirs, the Prince-Bishopric of Würzburg is obliged to pay the family’s female heirs 2,000 Reichstaler when these revenues revert to it.

Seal: The bishop, with his secret seal.

Notes: Abstract (18th century).
